{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-awesome-all-timeline-js","path":"/2021/07/25/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"title":"Track Awesome List"}},"allAwesomeItem":{"nodes":[{"awesomeListRepo":"awesome-css-group/awesome-css","categoryHTML":"<h2>Code Style Guidelines 📖</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://sass-guidelin.es/\">Sass Guidelines</a> by <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KittyGiraudel\">Kitty Giraudel</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T20:08:18.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"awesome-css-group/awesome-css","categoryHTML":"<h2>Twitter 🛰️</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://twitter.com/KittyGiraudel\">Kitty Giraudel</a> - Non-binary accessibility &#x26; diversity advocate, frontend developer, author.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T20:08:18.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>Videos</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9YdxhhgJvrE\">On .NET Live - Building Beautiful Blazor apps with Tailwind CSS</a> - <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Duration:%20-118%20min-%230094FF?style=flat-square&#x26;cacheSeconds=maxAge&#x26;logo=youtube\" alt=\"duration\"> June 17, 2021 - In this session on On .NET Live, Chris Sainty(@chris_sainty) will be showing us how to style our applications using Tailwind CSS as well as how to integrated the Blazored component libraries.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T18:20:24.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>Videos</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5fbzxjUUKUM\">Introduction to .NET MAUI Blazor | The Xamarin Show</a> - <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Duration:%20-19%20min-%230094FF?style=flat-square&#x26;cacheSeconds=maxAge&#x26;logo=youtube\" alt=\"duration\"> June 17, 2021 - Blazor enables building client-side web UI with .NET, but sometimes you need more than what the web platform offers. Sometimes you need full access to the native capabilities of the device. You can now host Blazor components in .NET MAUI apps to build cross-platform native apps using web UI. The components run natively in the .NET process and render web UI to an embedded web view control using a local interop channel. This hybrid approach gives you the best of native and the web. Your components can access native functionality through the .NET platform, and they render standard web UI. .NET MAUI Blazor apps can run anywhere .NET MAUI can (Windows, Mac, iOS, and Android) although our primary focus for .NET 6 is on desktop scenarios.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T18:20:24.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>Videos</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hz8i2HPSPts\">ASP.NET Community Standup - Build apps for Microsoft Teams with Blazor</a> - <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Duration:%20-76%20min-%230094FF?style=flat-square&#x26;cacheSeconds=maxAge&#x26;logo=youtube\" alt=\"duration\"> June 15, 2021 - Learn how to build apps for Microsoft Teams using the Teams Toolkit, .NET, and Blazor. <a href=\"https://www.theurlist.com/aspnet-standup-2021-06-15\">Community links</a>.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T18:20:24.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>Videos</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z9lkKnzJgD8\">The .NET Docs Show - Scenario testing Blazor Single-Page Apps</a> - <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Duration:%20-66%20min-%230094FF?style=flat-square&#x26;cacheSeconds=maxAge&#x26;logo=youtube\" alt=\"duration\"> June 28, 2021 - Cover all the bases and use test scenarios to improve the quality of your test coverage in Blazor applications.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T18:15:26.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>Videos</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Xzx7Cm9ykg\">Let's Learn .NET - Blazor</a> - <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Duration:%20-120%20min-%230094FF?style=flat-square&#x26;cacheSeconds=maxAge&#x26;logo=youtube\" alt=\"duration\"> June 25, 2021 - Blazor lets you build interactive web UIs using C# instead of JavaScript. Blazor apps are composed of reusable web UI components implemented using C#, HTML, and CSS. Both client and server code is written in C#, allowing you to share code and libraries. Together, we will learn all about Blazor and why you would use it to build web apps, and then we will build our first client web app with Blazor and .NET.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T18:15:26.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>Videos</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EUOimtP78jQ\">On .NET Live - Building Reactive UIs with Blazor</a> - <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Duration:%20-78%20min-%230094FF?style=flat-square&#x26;cacheSeconds=maxAge&#x26;logo=youtube\" alt=\"duration\"> June 24, 2021 - In this live session, Rodney Littles II shows us how to build Blazor applications with the ReactiveUI framework.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T18:15:26.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>Videos</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hKxciQMxueI\">ASP.NET Community Standup - Building with Blazor: Powered4.tv</a> - <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Duration:%20-78%20min-%230094FF?style=flat-square&#x26;cacheSeconds=maxAge&#x26;logo=youtube\" alt=\"duration\"> July 13, 2021 - Powered4.tv is a video-on-demand service that leverages Blazor WASM. In this episode of the Blazor community standup, we'll talk with product engineer Steve Pierce about the successes and stories behind using Blazor WASM for Powered4.tv.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T18:11:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>Videos</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q4D5NffKTIk\">On .NET Live - Secrets of building Blazor Components</a> - <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Duration:%20-80%20min-%230094FF?style=flat-square&#x26;cacheSeconds=maxAge&#x26;logo=youtube\" alt=\"duration\"> June 10, 2021 - This session with Ed Charbeneau is about building components for Blazor.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T18:08:58.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"APA-Technology-Division/urban-and-regional-planning-resources","categoryHTML":"<h2>Educational and Informational Resources</h2><h3>Literature Resources</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://www.trb.org/NCHRP/NCHRP.aspx\">NCHRP</a> - The National Cooperative Highway Research Program is developed on the basis of research needs identified by chief administrators and other staff of the highway and transportation departments, by committees of AASHTO, and by FHWA. Topics of the highest merit are selected by the AASHTO Special Committee on Research and Innovation (R&#x26;I), and each year R&#x26;I's recommendations are proposed to the AASHTO Board of Directors, the National Academies, and FHWA.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T18:01:14.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"meirwah/awesome-incident-response","categoryHTML":"<h2>IR tools Collection</h2><h3>Books</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Intelligence-Driven-Incident-Response-Outwitting-Adversary-ebook-dp-B074ZRN5T7/dp/B074ZRN5T7\">Intelligence-Driven Incident Response</a> - By Scott J. Roberts, Rebekah Brown.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-25T17:02:33.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"jaywcjlove/awesome-mac","categoryHTML":"<h2>Utilities</h2><h4>General Tools</h4>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Melvin-Abraham/Google-Assistant-Unofficial-Desktop-Client\">Google Assistant (Unofficial Desktop Client)</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/Melvin-Abraham/Google-Assistant-Unofficial-Desktop-Client\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sa